er> <kind>A</kind> </document-id><sources><source category="A"  name="SEA"  created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit><patcit ucid="JP-8157352-A"  status="new"><document-id status="new" format="epo"><country>JP</country><doc-number>8157352</doc-number><kind>A</kind></document-id><sources><source category="A" name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit><patcit ucid="US-4063017-A" status="new"><document-id status="new" format="epo"><country>US</country><doc-number>4063017</doc-number><kind>A</kind></document-id><sources><source category="A" name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit></patent-citations><non-patent-citations><nplcit status="new"><text>See also references of EP     1178108A1</text><sources><source name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></nplcit></non-patent-citations></citations></technical-data><parties><applicants><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>UYAMA SHIZUO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>UYAMA, SHIZUO</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>UYAMA SHIZUO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>UYAMA, SHIZUO</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A detergent composition which comprises inorganic particles and a soap such as a soda soap, wherein the inorganic particles are ones obtained by adding a pineapple juice to zeolite, calcium carbonate, silica, a ceramic powder, a fossil alga powder, a seashell powder, etc. and fermenting the juice to fix a pineapple enzyme to the inorganic material.  The composition causes no water pollution unlike synthetic detergents and is effective in avoiding the water pollution caused by wastewater resulting from cleaning.  In addition, due to the positive water-cleaning ability of the pineapple enzyme, the composition cleans the inside of a drainage piping, a sewage purifier tank, etc. to improve their functions.  Thus, water pollution can be mitigated.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne une composition détergente renfermant des particules inorganiques et un savon tel qu'un savon de soude. Les particules sont obtenues par addition d'un jus d'ananas dans une zéolite, un carbonate de calcium, un silicium, une poudre céramique, une poudre d'algues fossiles, une poudre de crustacés, etc. et par fermentation du jus de manière à fixer une enzyme d'ananas sur la matière inorganique. La composition ne pollue par les eaux à la différence des détergents synthétiques et permet d'éviter la pollution de l'eau causée par les déchets issus du nettoyage. En outre, grâce à la capacité de nettoyage à l'eau dont fait preuve l'enzyme d'ananas, la composition nettoie l'intérieur de canalisations d'évacuation, de réservoirs d'épuration des eaux d'égouts, etc. de manière à améliorer leur fonctionnement.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>